    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d657">

                <pb facs="0884" n="872" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg872"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611B.003/3–1846</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Resident Commissioner of the Philippines</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Romulo</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-03-18">March 18, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Secretary Byrnes</hi>: I have the honor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of your letter dated March 12, 1946,<anchor n="20"
                        xml:id="d657-f1"/> concerning the possibility of extending, after July 4,
                    1946, the application of the appropriate treaties and agreements of the United
                    States in force with other countries wherein rights of the Philippines are
                    protected in those countries.</p>
                <p>A copy of your letter has been transmitted by pouch to Manila. Directly the
                    comments of my Government are received with respect to the problems indicated in
                    your communication, I will be happy to inform you. In the meantime, I should
                    like to take advantage of your kind offer to discuss the question of existing
                    commercial treaty coverage of the Philippines and other phases of the general
                    problem with appropriate officers of the Department.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carlos</hi> P. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Romulo</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
